string.text:
The temple entrance has been disabled because Burning Empires could not load a valid culture-specific temple scene and religion visibility level.

What happened:
{REASON}

Configuration involved:
Settlement: {SETTLEMENT}
Culture: {CULTURE}
Religion: {RELIGION}
Scene: {SCENE}
Requested level: {LEVEL}
Fallback level: {FALLBACK}

What the program did:
The temple menu entry was hidden so the player cannot enter an incorrect or empty scene. No settlement, religion, population, save, or scene data was changed.

How to fix it:
Open BE ModuleData Source Files/BEData/be_temple_scenes.json and correct the listed culture, religion, scene, or level mapping. Confirm that SceneObj/{SCENE}/scene.xscene contains the requested level, then run BE ModuleData Builder/BEModuleDataBuilder.exe validate, dry-run, and pack. Start a new test session and check the temple entrance again.

This save contains Burning Empires external-data metadata, but the pre-load validation could not be completed. The game has cancelled loading so that the campaign save and its external population, religion, Wonder, Historical Campaign, and custom data cannot be combined incorrectly.

Save: {SAVE_NAME}
Error type: {ERROR_TYPE}
Details: {ERROR_MESSAGE}

Do not overwrite this save. Keep both the original .sav file and the matching BurningEmpires\BESavedata folder, then review the Burning Empires runtime log or report these details to the development team.

This save uses Burning Empires data version {0}. It can be loaded by migrating its module data to version {1}.
Modules to migrate: {2}
Migration runs on a deep copy and is committed only after every module validates. The original save will not be overwritten. After the world opens, provide a new Save As name before using any ordinary save command.

Bannerlord deleted the selected save, but Burning Empires could not safely prove that the complete campaign directory was obsolete.

Campaign ID: {CAMPAIGN_ID}
Deleted save slot: {SAVE_NAME}
Reason: {REASON}

The exact deleted slot remains protected by its deletion tombstone. Other campaign data was preserved instead of being guessed or recursively deleted.

Burning Empires could not remove external data after Bannerlord confirmed that a save was deleted.

What happened:
The original .sav was deleted, but Windows refused to remove part of the matching Burning Empires external data. The deletion tombstone remains active, so delayed save tasks and recovery data are blocked from restoring the deleted slot.

Affected campaign: {CAMPAIGN_ID}
Affected save slot: {SAVE_NAME}
Remaining path: {PATH}
Technical reason: {REASON}

What the program did:
Other saves remain available. Burning Empires will not load or rewrite the deleted slot from an old snapshot.

What to do:
Close Bannerlord, confirm that no editor or backup program is using the listed path, then delete that path manually. Do not delete other campaign directories.

Bannerlord deleted the selected .sav file, but Burning Empires could not finish synchronizing the matching external-data deletion.

What happened:
An unexpected file or index error interrupted external cleanup after the original save was deleted.

Campaign ID: {CAMPAIGN_ID}
Save slot: {SAVE_NAME}
Technical reason: {REASON}

What the program did:
The error was contained so that it cannot terminate the game or alter another save. Existing external files were left in place when their ownership could not be confirmed.

What to do:
Close Bannerlord, inspect BESavedata/campaigns/{CAMPAIGN_ID}, and remove only the folder for the deleted slot if it remains. Keep every other campaign and slot.

Burning Empires disabled new Government, state-religion proposal, player-founding religion, and religion-conversion features for this session because BEData/{FILE} could not be used. Existing kingdom and hero religion save data was not changed.
What happened: {REASON}
How to fix it: Correct BE ModuleData Source Files/BEData/{FILE}, then run BE ModuleData Builder validate, dry-run, and pack before restarting the game.

{ITEM}
Progress: {PROGRESS}%
Remaining productive hours: {HOURS}
Started in: {TOWN}
Craftspeople: {ARTISANS}

Field or slot: {FIELD}
Configured object ID: {OBJECT_ID}
Fallback used: {FALLBACK}
